### Example B — Telehealth patient intake portal

**Brief:** Clinic wants a patient portal for pre-visit intake: forms, insurance
card upload, symptom questionnaire, and secure messaging with the care team.
Must integrate with their existing EHR via a REST API.

**Estimate:**

## Summary
Patient intake portal with secure forms, document upload, and EHR integration.

## Phases
- Patient auth and secure session handling — 14h — 875 EUR
- Intake forms and symptom questionnaire — 22h — 1,375 EUR
- Insurance card upload and storage — 12h — 750 EUR
- Secure messaging with care team — 18h — 1,125 EUR
- EHR REST API integration — 24h — 1,500 EUR
- Testing and QA (incl. HIPAA-aware review) — 20h — 1,250 EUR

## Totals
- Hours: 110 — Cost: 6,875 EUR — Team: 1 backend developer, 1 frontend developer —
  Duration: 6 weeks

## Risks
- Assumes the EHR API already exposes the required intake endpoints; no EHR-side
  changes are scoped.
